    "extraction_notes": "Single SoA table (ISA Section 1.3) printed over document pages 10-13 under a header (with the shaded Telephone Visit row and the Procedures band) reprinted on every page; p.9 carries the Section 1.3 heading and the intro text, captured as table-wide note g1. The table pages are glyph-spread: every activity label and Notes cell was rebuilt from the glyph stream and read again against the rendered page (§1c). Marks verified by pdftotext -bbox column binning (no disagreement with the visual read). Cell boundaries from raster rule lines (§1d). Notes column cells captured as annotations with synthesised markers n1-n19; footnotes a, b, c on the Telephone Visit marks are printed inside that row's Notes cell, a and b wholly covered by CCI boxes. Abbreviation list dropped. Redaction: footnotes a and b, part of one row on p.12, and the Notes cell of 'Participant returns device'.",
    "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
  },
  "table_metadata": {
    "table_number": 1,
    "table_type": "main_soa",
    "table_title": "Schedule of Activities (SoA)",
    "table_purpose": "ISA NP03 (LY3556050, diabetic peripheral neuropathic pain) schedule: visits and procedures unique to the ISA, on top of the master CPMP and DPNP DSA CPMP(3) SoAs; V3-V7 and ED shared with the master, two telephone visits after V3 and a follow-up visit V801 added",
    "page_start": 9,
    "page_end": 13,
    "notes": "One label column (L=1); data columns at positions 2-8 (V3 -> 2, V4 -> 3, V5 -> 4, V6 -> 5, V7 -> 6, ED -> 7, V801 -> 8); the right-hand Notes column is not a schedule column. The shaded 'Telephone Visit' row is printed with the header on every page and is recorded as header row 5 (see review item D1); it marks V3 (footnotes a, b, both redacted) and V801 (footnote c). The 'Procedures' band under it is reprinted on every page: a column-label band, not an activity (row position 6, left out). Typed main_soa: every participant randomised into this ISA passes through it in sequence. It is a delta schedule: the intro text says it shows only what is unique to the ISA, so the participant's full schedule is this table plus the master and DSA SoAs; recorded here and in g1. Section bands 'Laboratory Tests and Sample Collection' and 'Participant Device' group the rows below them. One row on p.12 is redacted in its label and V3-ED cells (its V801 and Notes cells are blank); its row position (26) is unassigned."
  },
